 x 1.2;3. 4 x 3.4 x 1.2;4. 3 x 2.2. x 0.5;5. unregistered","Zych, I.","","5135","wood","spr","2011-03-08 09:33:39","worked (collective)","","103","Zych, I.(2009); Wójcik, B.(2011)","BE09-57_007_PB016_wood_, d","1. complete(?); good condition;2. good condition;3. some salt encrustation and fluffing of wood;4.good condition;5. good condition.","","5+5","","See:1. brailing ring BE09-57/007/031;2. brailing ring BE09-57/007/032;3. shaft(?) fragment BE09-57/007/033;4. handle BE09-57/007/034;5. slat(?) BE09-57/007/035;","","Zych, I.; wood identification Zieliński, J.","","","","""pp","0587-Q-026","","2009_02_03","","Sectioned piece of shaft(?), cut across length from thick branch, sides pared down asymmetrically, off center, but following flattened octagonal shape. Paring of sides irregular. Nail shaft hole, square, roughly 0.3x0.5 at core center of branch. Thickness uneven","3.5 x 3; H. 1.6-1.9","Zych, I.; inking Woźniak, M.; digitizing Puszkarski, M.","","5136","Pinewood (Abies cilicica).","","2011-10-04 23:44:24","shaft(?)","BE09-57/007/033","103","Zych, I.","BE09-57_007_033_a, d.JPG","accreted deposit on one side, otherwise well preserved","","1","","","","Zych, I.; wood identification Zieliński, J.","","","","""pp","0588-Q-027","","2009_02_03","","Long truncated conical shape,doubling the diameter both ways. Cut from length of branch. Top of handle worked concavely, leaving round knob in the center raised only by depth of carving around it (minimally 0.1mm). Mounting end has 3 cm long slot in center, cut to the outside, inside end squared evenly, 0.1 mm wide. Pierced transversely through slot two holes about 1 cm apart, traces in wood each about 1-2 mm thick, but the peg must have been slightly bigger. Width of mounting element could have been 1.0 at the maximum (short end), if it did not stick out.","L. 7.2; W. 2.25-1.25; H. 1.1-0.5","Zych, I.; inking Woźniak, M.; digitizing Puszkarski, M.","","5137","wood","spr","2011-03-07 11:43:40","handle","BE09-57/